    "review_summary": "Accuracy: 7 of the 304 live condition sets were examined, the first six and the one bacterial set. They select RING-finger, U-box, Bre1, SIAH and plant ATL families and the bacterial novel E3 ligase effectors, and every reviewed match carries EC 2.3.2.27 (254 of 254, summed over sets). The rule contains no HECT-domain condition. The other 297 sets were not checked against proteins. Meaning and parsimony: EC 2.3.2.27 names one enzyme class, RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferases, and six of the seven recorded sets select families of that class. Two units do not belong to it by mechanism. Set 12 selects IpaH/SspH-type bacterial effectors, which UniProt records as forming a glycyl thioester intermediate on an active-site cysteine, unlike RING and U-box ligases. And a scan of the names of all conditions in the live rule found one set built from three PIAS FunFams (not among the sets recorded here): it gives the ubiquitin transferase reaction to E3 SUMO-protein ligases, on the strength of the EC number that Swiss-Prot puts on PIAS4 alone among the PIAS proteins.",
