    "description": "Assigns the catalytic activity alpha-D-galactose = beta-D-galactose (RHEA:28675, EC 5.1.3.3, galactose mutarotase) through two alternative condition sets: InterPro IPR008183 and IPR011013 in Metazoa, or CATH FunFam 2.70.98.10:FF:000003 in Eukaryota.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: both live condition sets were checked against Swiss-Prot on 2026-11-09. Each matches six reviewed entries and all six carry EC 5.1.3.3 (GALM orthologues, e.g. human Q96C23). The Metazoa restriction in set 1 is needed, because across all taxa IPR008183 (Aldose 1-/Glucose-6-phosphate 1-epimerase) has 32 Swiss-Prot members of which only 18 carry EC 5.1.3.3. TrEMBL matches were counted but not inspected. Meaning and parsimony: the two sets select one biological unit, the animal galactose mutarotase GALM, and the reaction assigned is the reaction that unit catalyses, so the rule is coherent. The six reviewed matches of set 2 are the same six entries as those of set 1; set 2 exists to reach non-metazoan eukaryotes through the narrower FunFam. The rule is small and each set does work.",
