    "description": "ARBA rule assigning the subcellular location \"Cytoplasmic vesicle, secretory vesicle, acrosome\" through 38 alternative condition sets, each a conjunction of family signatures with a taxon condition.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 38 condition sets were turned into UniProtKB queries. In every set, every reviewed match carries a curated acrosome location, so the rule reproduces Swiss-Prot within animals. One set does not stay within animals: set 10 (MORN repeat-containing protein 3) is restricted only to Eukaryota minus five plant, fungal and amoebozoan taxa, and it puts the acrosome location on 333 proteins of trypanosomatids, alveolates and other protists, which have no acrosome. Meaning and parsimony: each set selects one family, and the shared statement is a location in an animal sperm organelle. For about fifteen sets the family is a widely expressed protein (dihydrolipoyl dehydrogenase, CDC42, RAB2, RAB6A, RACGAP1, golgin A1, the epithelial sodium channel alpha subunit, CD46 and others) whose acrosome location is a secondary site reported in sperm; the statement is true of the reviewed members but is not what those families are about. Set 5 adds no protein beyond set 19.",
