    "id": "ARBA00005098",
    "rule_id": "ARBA00005098",
    "description": "Assigns the pathway comment \"Nitrogen metabolism; urea cycle; L-ornithine and urea from L-arginine: step 1/1\" (the arginase step) through nine alternative condition sets: InterPro arginase signatures in Chordata, a PANTHER subfamily in Bacteria, and seven CATH FunFams of superfamily 3.40.800.10, each with its own taxon.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all nine live condition sets were checked against Swiss-Prot on 2026-11-09. Every reviewed match of every set carries the pathway comment (16, 13, 9, 8, 6, 6, 6, 4 and 3 entries for sets 1 to 9). TrEMBL matches were counted but not inspected. Meaning and parsimony: sets 1 to 8 select one unit, the arginases, for which the arginase step of the urea cycle is the right comment. Set 9 selects a different unit. Its three mammalian Swiss-Prot matches are AGMAT orthologues (human Q9BSE5), which Swiss-Prot names guanidino acid hydrolase; the record says the enzyme prefers taurocyamine and guanidino propanoic and butanoic acids and \"Metabolizes L-arginine with low efficiency\", and its pathway comment is a curator inference (ECO:0000305). The comment is therefore true of set 9 only through a weak side activity, and a rule that propagates it to 174 UniProtKB entries presents a guanidino acid hydrolase as a urea-cycle arginase. Among the arginase sets, sets 3 and 8 have no reviewed match outside set 2 and sets 4 and 7 none outside set 1, which is mild redundancy.",
