    "description": "Assigns the UniProt keyword Methyltransferase (KW-0489) from 624 alternative condition sets of InterPro, FunFam, PANTHER and taxon conditions.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: the rule assigns the keyword Methyltransferase (KW-0489) from 624 alternative condition sets. On 2026-11-12 each of the 624 sets of the rule as fetched on 2026-11-10 was turned into a UniProtKB query and counted against Swiss-Prot. Every set has reviewed matches (2 to 844 per set, median 8; 29761 summed over sets) and no set has a reviewed match that lacks the keyword. TrEMBL matches were not inspected, and the individual sets are not recorded in this review. Meaning and parsimony: the keyword names an enzyme class and the sets select methyltransferase families, one or a few sets each. A systematic sample of 12 sets (every 52nd) gave twelve different families: rRNA methyltransferases RsmH, RlmC and RsmA, catechol O-methyltransferases, the tetrahydromethanopterin S-methyltransferase subunit A, fungal polyketide synthases keyworded as methyltransferases, fungal secondary-metabolite methyltransferases, betaine-homocysteine S-methyltransferase, SETDB histone methyltransferases, NSUN2, PRMT9 and the citrate synthase lysine methyltransferase. The keyword is the level at which the class is defined, so a rule spanning many families is what a keyword rule is for. Redundancy between sets was not measured.",
