    "id": "ARBA00022722",
    "rule_id": "ARBA00022722",
    "description": "Assigns the UniProt keyword Nuclease (KW-0540) through 538 alternative condition sets built from InterPro entries, PANTHER families and CATH FunFams. 326 sets are conjunctions of two or more conditions and 153 carry a taxon condition.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: the first 287 of 538 live condition sets (CS1 to CS287) were queried against Swiss-Prot on 2026-11-09; each has reviewed matches and every reviewed match inspected carries the keyword Nuclease (KW-0540). On 2026-11-12 the remaining 251 sets, which this review does not record, were counted by UniProtKB query from the same rule snapshot: all have reviewed matches (966 summed over sets) and 250 have none lacking the keyword. One does: the set FunFam 1.20.58.190:FF:000001 AND FunFam 1.20.58.200:FF:000002 matches six reviewed entries, all translin (for example human Q15631 and mouse Q62348), and none carries the keyword. Translin is the non-catalytic partner of translin-associated protein X in the C3PO complex; Swiss-Prot gives the keywords Endonuclease and Nuclease and EC 3.1.26.- to the partner (Q99598) and not to translin. Of 1166 UniProtKB entries matching that set, 1160 unreviewed entries carry the keyword, for example Q7JVK6 with evidence ARBA:ARBA00022722. TrEMBL matches of the other sets were not inspected. Meaning and parsimony: the keyword names an enzyme class and the sets select nuclease families, one or a few sets per family. In a systematic sample of 12 recorded sets, 5 select endonucleases only (RNase HII, XPF, Slx1, retrotransposon Gag-Pol, hantavirus nucleoprotein), 6 exonucleases only (DNA polymerase I, Rrp6-like, Apollo, AddA, archaeal Rrp41 and a PANTHER subfamily of 3'-5' exonucleases) and 1 a family that Swiss-Prot keywords as Nuclease without a subclass (VapC toxins). Nuclease is the parent of Endonuclease and Exonuclease in the keyword hierarchy and UniProt shows parent and child together, so the general keyword is the expected companion of the specific one, not a replacement for it.",
