    "id": "ARBA00022759",
    "rule_id": "ARBA00022759",
    "description": "Assigns the UniProt keyword Endonuclease (KW-0255) through 320 alternative condition sets. Each set is one to three InterPro entries or PANTHER families, in about a third of the sets with a taxon.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: 11 of the 320 live condition sets were examined, the first six and five that contain a domain shared with non-nuclease proteins. In each, every reviewed match carries the Endonuclease keyword KW-0255 (4008 of 4008, summed over sets). The remaining 309 sets were not checked against proteins. Meaning and parsimony: the keyword names an enzyme class, and ten of the eleven recorded sets select a family whose signature is that of the nuclease itself (RNase HII, YbeY, RuvC, RNase P protein, RNase III, FEN1, NendoU, UvdE, plant MORC). Set 10 is different: its only signature is the reverse transcriptase domain, in Pararnavirae, and it reaches the keyword because full-length retroviral and pararetroviral polymerase polyproteins also contain RNase H. Of the 30500 unreviewed entries it matches, 28740 are fragments and 20788 are at most 400 residues long with no RNase H signature, so the set labels reverse transcriptase fragments as endonucleases.",
