    "rule_id": "ARBA00022801",
    "description": "ARBA rule assigning the UniProt keyword Hydrolase (KW-0378) through 4171 alternative condition sets built from InterPro, PANTHER and taxon conditions.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 4171 served condition sets were compared with Swiss-Prot keyword use. 4170 sets match reviewed entries, and in all but one of them every reviewed match carries the keyword Hydrolase (130233 of 130239 reviewed matches summed over sets). The exception is set 2549, two FunFams whose reviewed members are translin: none of the six carries the keyword, yet the 1160 unreviewed translins it matches all receive Hydrolase from this rule. One set (389) matches no UniProtKB entry at all. The 44 sets recorded here in detail (four from the first pass and a random sample of 40) all agree with Swiss-Prot. Meaning and parsimony: the rule does what its label says, selecting hydrolase families one by one and giving them the class-level keyword. The keyword is broad by design; UniProt keywords are hierarchical and an entry carries the class keyword beside a narrower one, so the 1759 sets that are also condition sets of rules for narrower keywords (Protease 689, Nuclease 355, Glycosidase 284, Helicase 201, Protein phosphatase 141 and others) still do work.",
