    "description": "Assigns the UniProt keyword Serine protease (KW-0720) through 244 alternative condition sets, each one to three InterPro entries or PANTHER families, in part with a taxon.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: the first 10 of the 244 live condition sets were examined. They select ClpP, subtilisin (peptidase S8), Lon, kallikrein-related trypsin-family and proteinase K-like families, and every reviewed match carries the Serine protease keyword KW-0720 (3533 of 3533, summed over sets). The other 234 sets were then scanned against Swiss-Prot (UniProtKB 2026_04): every set has reviewed matches, and all 8,032 reviewed matches summed over the 244 sets carry the keyword; the counts are recorded per set. Meaning and parsimony: Serine protease is a catalytic-class keyword with no child keywords, and the sampled sets resolve into four serine peptidase clans whose members share exactly that property. Several sets address one family with different signatures and overlap heavily, but each sampled set still matches at least one reviewed entry that its sibling does not, so none is shown to do no work.",
