    "review_summary": "Accuracy: every one of the 908 live condition sets was put through one check in this pass, namely whether its Swiss-Prot matches carry the keyword (UniProtKB queries, November 2026); 31 sets were also read in detail and are recorded. All 908 sets match Swiss-Prot entries (2 at least, median 10). In 907 sets every Swiss-Prot match carries KW-0456 Lyase; summed over sets, 54,395 of 54,396 matches do. The exception is set 150, the ACMSD family: 27 of its 28 Swiss-Prot matches are decarboxylases or hydratases, and the 28th, A6KWY3 (LGAB_PHOV8), is an experimentally characterised L-galactono-1,5-lactonase (EC 3.1.1.126), a hydrolase. The rule gives the keyword to TrEMBL copies of that enzyme: I8ZCI2, identical to A6KWY3 over all 308 residues, carries Lyase with ARBA00023239 as its source. Meaning and parsimony: the keyword names EC class 4, and the sets select lyase families: in the 30-set sample the reviewed matches are carbon-carbon lyases (12 sets), carbon-oxygen lyases (12) and other EC 4 subclasses (6). That is the level at which the keyword exists, so the rule is coherent. No set is empty and none duplicates or contains another.",
