    "description": "Assigns GO:0051998 (protein carboxyl O-methyltransferase activity) through six alternative condition sets covering three enzyme families: isoprenylcysteine carboxyl methyltransferases (sets 1, 3, 4), protein-L-isoaspartate O-methyltransferases (sets 2, 5) and leucine carboxyl methyltransferase 1 (set 6).",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all six live condition sets were examined. They match 40 reviewed entries and every one carries GO:0051998 (protein carboxyl O-methyltransferase activity) or a descendant, 39 by manual evidence, so the annotation is true for every family the rule covers. Meaning and parsimony: the six sets resolve into three unrelated enzyme families, each of which has its own curated child term: isoprenylcysteine carboxyl methyltransferase (sets 1, 3, 4), GO:0004671 (protein C-terminal S-isoprenylcysteine carboxyl O-methyltransferase activity); protein-L-isoaspartate O-methyltransferase (sets 2, 5), GO:0004719 (protein-L-isoaspartate (D-aspartate) O-methyltransferase activity); and leucine carboxyl methyltransferase 1 (set 6), GO:0018423 (protein C-terminal leucine carboxyl O-methyltransferase activity). The consequent is the shared parent and says less than any of them. Four of the sets are already matched by rules asserting a more specific term, so they emit nothing, and InterPro2GO maps both InterPro entries of set 1 to GO:0004671.",
    "action": "SPLIT",
