    "id": "ARBA00026698",
    "rule_id": "ARBA00026698",
    "description": "Assigns GO:0007034 vacuolar transport through 40 alternative condition sets, each a conjunction of InterPro or CATH FunFam signatures with a taxon. The sets cover ESCRT-III/Snf7-family proteins, ESCRT-I and ESCRT-II subunits, Vps4, sortilin/Vps10 and plant vacuolar sorting receptors, vacuolar syntaxins, GGA/VHS adaptors, NEDD4/Rsp5-type ubiquitin ligases and a few other families.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 40 live condition sets were examined. Twenty-six match Swiss-Prot entries, and in every one of them at least one matched entry carries GO:0007034 (vacuolar transport) or a descendant with experimental evidence; no matched Swiss-Prot entry lacks the term. The other 14 sets are Archaea or Bacteria copies of eukaryotic sets and match no UniProtKB entry. Meaning and parsimony: the working sets all concern traffic to the vacuole or lysosome, but they fall into four groups that curated annotation distinguishes: protein targeting to the vacuole by sorting receptors (4 sets), the ESCRT and multivesicular body route from late endosomes (10), lysosomal transport in animals (9) and Golgi-to-vacuole SNAREs and adaptors (3). Each group has a child term of the consequent, and rules for three of those terms already match 8 of the working sets exactly. A third of the rule (14 sets) can never fire, and set 1 repeats an InterPro2GO mapping.",
