    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all five condition sets of the rule as served on 2026-11-10 were turned into UniProtKB queries. In every set the reviewed matches are NAD kinases by curated EC number (698 of 704 across the sets), and sets 1, 4 and 5 include members with experimental GO:0003951 (NAD+ kinase activity) annotations. The soft spot is in set 1, which also matches the mitochondrial NADH kinase POS5 and its S. pombe ortholog, curated as NADH kinases (EC 2.7.1.86). Meaning and parsimony: the sets select one enzyme family, NAD kinase, including the metazoan mitochondrial NADK2 branch, and the consequent is its defining activity. Nearly all of the rule repeats InterPro2GO, which maps IPR002504 (NAD kinase) to the same term: sets 1, 2 and 3 match no entry without that mapping, set 4 matches 6 and set 5 matches 45.",
