    "id": "ARBA00027169",
    "rule_id": "ARBA00027169",
    "description": "Assigns GO:0120114 Sm-like protein family complex through 27 alternative condition sets of InterPro and CATH FunFam signatures, some with a taxon. The sets cover Sm and Lsm proteins and other protein components of the U1, U2, U5, U6, U7 and U11/U12 snRNPs.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 27 live condition sets were examined. Every set matches Swiss-Prot entries, and in each at least one matched entry carries GO:0120114 (Sm-like protein family complex) or a descendant with experimental evidence; no matched Swiss-Prot entry lacks the term. Spliceosomal snRNPs are subclasses of the term (GO:0030532 (small nuclear ribonucleoprotein complex) is_a GO:0120114 (Sm-like protein family complex)), so snRNP proteins without an Sm fold, such as SF3B1, PRPF8, BRR2 and Snu114, are covered correctly. Meaning and parsimony: 24 of the 27 sets (4 to 27) select proteins of a particular snRNP or of the Lsm2-8 ring, and for all 24 a rule asserting a more specific term already uses the same signatures: ARBA00033820 asserts GO:0030532 (small nuclear ribonucleoprotein complex) for 22 of them and ARBA00089766 asserts GO:0120115 (Lsm2-8 complex) for sets 5 and 6, with further rules for the individual U1, U2, U5, U6 and U7 snRNPs. Those sets emit nothing from this rule. Only sets 1 to 3, which are InterPro signatures spanning both Sm and Lsm paralogs, do work, and for them the umbrella term is the right level.",
