    "description": "Assigns GO:0008236 (serine-type peptidase activity) through 45 alternative condition sets built from InterPro entries, PANTHER families and CATH FunFams, most with a taxon. The sets cover coagulation and complement proteases, trypsin-family enzymes, subtilisin-like proprotein convertases, HtrA/DegP proteases, tripeptidyl peptidases and others.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 45 live condition sets were checked against Swiss-Prot. They match 292 reviewed entries and every one carries GO:0008236 (serine-type peptidase activity) or a descendant, 225 by manual evidence. Set 13 is wrong: it selects BMP1 and the tolloid-like proteins, which are zinc metalloproteases and carry a serine-type endopeptidase term only through a Reactome TAS annotation. Set 5 has the same contaminant: BMP1 (P13497) is one of its nine reviewed matches. Meaning and parsimony: of the 45 sets, 39 select serine endopeptidases (trypsin-fold coagulation, complement, kallikrein and granzyme proteases, subtilisin-like proprotein convertases, HtrA/DegP, rhomboid and others) whose members are curated to the child term GO:0004252 (serine-type endopeptidase activity). Three select tripeptidyl peptidases, curated to GO:0008240 (tripeptidyl-peptidase activity); one selects carboxypeptidase Y, curated to GO:0004185 (serine-type carboxypeptidase activity); one selects L,D-transpeptidases, curated to GO:0071972 (peptidoglycan L,D-transpeptidase activity). The consequent is the parent that hides the endo/exo distinction every unit has. 21 sets are already covered by rules for those child terms and emit nothing.",
