    "rule_id": "ARBA00027723",
    "description": "ARBA rule assigning GO:0016740 transferase activity through 1340 alternative condition sets built from InterPro, CATH FunFam, PANTHER and taxon conditions.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: the first pass examined no condition set. Fourteen of the 1340 served sets were drawn at random (Python random.sample, seed 4, over set numbers) and checked against curated annotations of their Swiss-Prot members; in every one a reviewed member carries a curated descendant of GO:0016740 (transferase activity), so the annotation is true for the sample and no false positive was found. The other 1326 sets were not checked. Meaning and parsimony: the term is the root of all transferase activities and says nothing about a protein whose reaction is known. The fourteen sets resolve into fourteen unrelated families (phage polymerases, plant UDP-glycosyltransferases, arginine kinase, malate synthase, sulfotransferases, histone acetyltransferases, protein kinases, aminotransferases, prenyl diphosphate synthases and others), each with its own curated activity term. rule_redundancy.tsv finds 1013 of 1340 sets already matched by a rule asserting a more specific term, so three quarters of the rule emits nothing.",
