    "description": "ARBA rule assigning GO:0006338 chromatin remodeling through 167 alternative condition sets built from InterPro, CATH FunFam, PANTHER and taxon conditions.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: nine of the 167 served condition sets were checked against curated annotations of their Swiss-Prot members (sets 1, 7, 13, 19, 46, 63, 108, 130 and 140). In each a reviewed member carries a curated term that is GO:0006338 (chromatin remodeling) or an is_a/part_of descendant, so no false positive was found; the earlier report of a false positive on human UBR7 was not reproducible. The other 158 sets were not checked. Meaning and parsimony: GO places histone modifying activities, ATP-dependent remodeler activity and heterochromatin formation under the term, so the rule is true across its sets, but it flattens units that each carry a more informative term: histone methyltransferases, class I histone deacetylases, Polycomb EZH1/EZH2 and DNA methyltransferase 1 (heterochromatin formation), CHD1 (nucleosome organization), transcription-coupled remodeling factors, a histone variant, and DNA topoisomerase I, whose defining process is outside the term. rule_redundancy.tsv finds 47 of 167 sets already matched by a rule asserting a more specific term.",
