    "description": "Assigns GO:0004175 (endopeptidase activity) through 104 alternative condition sets built from InterPro entries, PANTHER families and CATH FunFams, most with a taxon. The sets cover caspases, papain-like and legumain cysteine peptidases, aspartic peptidases, proteasome subunits, signal peptidases, trypsin- and subtilisin-like serine peptidases and several metallopeptidase families.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 104 live condition sets were checked against Swiss-Prot. They match 1063 reviewed entries and every one carries GO:0004175 (endopeptidase activity) or a descendant, 630 by manual evidence. One set is weakly founded: set 14 is the single InterPro entry IPR003675, which matches 56399 unreviewed entries; of its 40 reviewed matches only the 10 CAAX prenyl protease 2 orthologues have a manual annotation. Meaning and parsimony: 99 of the 104 sets select a family whose members are curated to one of the catalytic-class children of the consequent: serine-type (35 sets), cysteine-type (15, plus 6 for the calcium-dependent calpain term), aspartic-type (13), metallo- (25) and threonine-type (5, the proteasome). Catalytic class is the first thing known about any of these families and is exactly what the consequent leaves out. Only five sets (CAAX prenyl protease 2, coronavirus replicase polyproteins, latrophilin-like proteins, a deubiquitinase FunFam, mitochondrial inner membrane protease) have no class term curated on the members looked up. 29 sets are already covered by rules for the class terms and emit nothing.",
