    "description": "ARBA rule that assigned GO:0046467 membrane lipid biosynthetic process through 51 alternative condition sets built from InterPro, CATH FunFam and taxon conditions. GO has made the term obsolete and UniProt no longer serves the rule.",
    "review_summary": "GO:0046467 is obsolete in GO, and UniProt returned 404 for this rule on 2026-11-09. The 51 condition sets recorded are those of the last version reviewed. Nine of them (sets 2, 5, 12, 15, 19, 26, 31, 37 and 45) were checked against Swiss-Prot members and their GO annotations. In each case a matched protein carries a curated annotation to a lipid biosynthetic process: the ceramidases, sphingomyelinase and glucosylceramidase are annotated to biosynthesis of their products ceramide and sphingosine; protein kinase D and the chloroplast phosphoglycerate kinases are annotated to sphingolipid and galactolipid biosynthesis; and the Bacteroidota set selects serine palmitoyltransferases. So these sets reflect existing annotations rather than fold-level errors. The other 42 sets were not checked. Meaning and parsimony were not judged in full because the rule is gone. From the nine checked sets the pattern is an umbrella term over unrelated units: sphingolipid hydrolases annotated to biosynthesis of their products, protein kinase D reached through a Reactome pathway statement, chloroplast phosphoglycerate kinases reached through one genetic study, and bacterial serine palmitoyltransferases.",
