    "description": "Assigns GO:0005778 (peroxisomal membrane) through 16 alternative condition sets covering peroxins (PEX2/10, PEX4, PEX11, PEX12, PEX13, PEX14 and the fungal DysF-domain peroxins), peroxisomal ABC transporters, PMP34 (SLC25A17), ATAD1, fatty acyl-CoA reductase, NBR1 and a Penicillium transporter FunFam, each with a taxon restriction.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 16 live condition sets were examined. They match 83 reviewed entries; 82 carry GO:0005778 (peroxisomal membrane) or a descendant, 77 by manual evidence. Fourteen sets are supported by experimental localisation of at least one reviewed match. Two are not sound: the NBR1 set rests on Reactome TAS annotations only, and the Penicillium transporter set selects a broad fungal drug-transporter FunFam whose reviewed match sorT (B6HNK5) is described by UniProt as a cell-membrane transporter. Meaning and parsimony: fourteen sets select integral or tightly associated proteins of the peroxisomal membrane (peroxins PEX2/10, PEX4, PEX11, PEX12, PEX13, PEX14 and the fungal DysF-domain peroxins; ABCD transporters; PMP34; ATAD1; FAR1), for which the consequent is the most informative component term. NBR1 (set 7) is a soluble autophagy receptor whose experimental locations are cytoplasm and lysosome, and set 12 is a species-restricted generic transporter FunFam. Sets 1, 2 and 3 each contain an InterPro entry that InterPro2GO already maps to the same term without a taxon limit, so they add nothing.",
