    "description": "Assigns GO:0048468 (cell development) through 392 alternative condition sets. Every set is a conjunction of one to three InterPro entries, PANTHER families or CATH FunFams with a taxon.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: the first 10 of the 392 live condition sets were examined. Six match reviewed entries, and 78 of 79 of those entries carry GO:0048468 (cell development) or a descendant, 48 by manual evidence. Four of the ten repeat the conditions of a neighbouring set for Archaea or Bacteria and match no UniProtKB entry. The other 382 sets were not checked against proteins. Meaning and parsimony: GO:0048468 has 672 descendants. The sampled sets are domain architectures (BTB with C2H2 zinc fingers, SH2 with SH3, the tyrosine phosphatase domain, hedgehog, peptidase M17) restricted to an animal clade, and their reviewed members reach the term through unrelated developmental phenotypes: axon guidance for Abl, Ptp69D, lola and Shh, spermatid development for the Drosophila sperm leucyl aminopeptidases and Dhh, photoreceptor development for ttk. The consequent is the common ancestor of those phenotype terms, not a property the architectures share. Across the whole rule, 103 sets of conditions occur three times, once each for Archaea, Bacteria and Eukaryota, so 206 of the 392 sets are copies of animal developmental families under prokaryotic taxa; all four such copies in the sample match nothing.",
