    "description": "Assigns GO:0016070 (RNA metabolic process) through 375 alternative condition sets built from InterPro entries, PANTHER families and CATH FunFams, about a quarter of them with a taxon.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: the first 10 of the 375 live condition sets were examined. They select aminoacyl-tRNA synthetases, Dicer-type RNase III helicases, pseudouridine synthases, terminal nucleotidyltransferases, plant RNA-editing factors, eL30-fold proteins and queuine tRNA-ribosyltransferases, and 2794 of 2794 reviewed matches carry GO:0016070 (RNA metabolic process) or a descendant. The other 365 sets were not checked against proteins. Meaning and parsimony: GO:0016070 has 507 descendants and is the root of nearly all RNA biology. The sampled sets resolve into seven unrelated units, and for each one curated annotation gives a far more specific descendant: tRNA aminoacylation, pre-miRNA processing, pseudouridine synthesis, RNA 3'-end processing, organellar RNA modification, rRNA processing and tRNA wobble guanine modification. No sampled unit is curated to the consequent itself. 289 of the rule's sets are already matched by rules asserting a more specific term, so most of the rule emits nothing, and what it does emit is the least informative thing that can be said about an RNA enzyme.",
