    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 19 live condition sets were examined. They match 86 reviewed entries; 85 carry GO:0005681 (spliceosomal complex) or a descendant, 70 by manual evidence. One set is wider than its evidence: set 2 requires only two generic DEAH-box helicase signatures in Taphrinomycotina, and three of its eight reviewed Schizosaccharomyces pombe matches carry the term only from this rule while PomBase places them in the nucleolus or cytosol. Meaning and parsimony: eighteen sets select subunits and stably associated factors of one machine (Sm core proteins, U1A and U2B'', spliceosomal DEAH-box helicases, PRP17, SNRNP40, cyclophilins, the exon junction factor MAGOH, branchpoint-binding protein and others), and the general complex term is the one curated on most of them, usually beside several stage-specific descendants, so it is the right level for a rule that spans stages. Set 2 is the exception. Three sets are covered by rules asserting more specific spliceosome terms, and InterPro2GO already maps an Sm F entry to the term.",
