    "description": "Assigns GO:0004438 phosphatidylinositol-3-phosphate phosphatase activity through two condition sets: CATH FunFam 2.30.29.30:FF:000038 in Primates (MTM1, MTMR1, MTMR2) and CATH FunFam 3.30.40.10:FF:000073 in Eukaryota (the FYVE-domain region of MTMR3 and MTMR4).",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: both live condition sets were checked against Swiss-Prot. Set 1 is supported: its 5 reviewed matches (MTM1, MTMR1, MTMR2) all carry GO:0004438 (phosphatidylinositol-3-phosphate phosphatase activity) with non-electronic evidence. Set 2 is not specific to myotubularins. Of its 19 reviewed matches, 6 are MTMR3 or MTMR4 experimentally annotated to the term, for example Q9NYA4 by IDA from PMID:11302699, and 13 are insect Lst2 homologues that have a FYVE domain but no phosphatase domain and carry the term only from this rule. In UniProtKB 126 of 3192 matches of set 2 lack IPR010569 (Myotubularin-like, phosphatase domain). Meaning and parsimony: the intended units are two branches of the myotubularin family, and GO:0004438 is the most informative molecular function term curated on both, with no descendants in GO. For those units the rule is coherent and minimal. Set 2 also selects a third, unrelated unit, the Lst2 FYVE proteins, whose curated function is phosphatidylinositol-3-phosphate binding and not hydrolysis, because its only signature is a FunFam of the FYVE region.",
