    "description": "Assigns GO:0140115 (export across plasma membrane) through 14 alternative condition sets that identify efflux transporters: bacterial SMR and Emr multidrug exporters, fungal MFS and ABC drug exporters, plant ABCB auxin transporters, metazoan ABCG2, sodium-exporting P-type ATPases, Na+/K+-ATPase alpha subunits, fungal Na+/H+ antiporters and Na+/Ca2+ exchangers.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all 14 live condition sets were examined by retrieving the Swiss-Prot entries that match the whole conjunction and looking up their curated annotations. Every set has at least one Swiss-Prot match with an experimental annotation to GO:0140115 (export across plasma membrane) or an is_a/part_of descendant. In several sets only some reviewed matches are annotated, for example 4 of 47 in set 3 and 2 of 8 in set 12. The curator concern in geneontology/go-annotation issue 6140 could not be read, so the set it refers to is not identified. Meaning and parsimony: the 14 sets select unrelated exporter families that share only the direction of transport. They resolve into multidrug efflux transporters, plant ABCB auxin exporters, sodium-exporting pumps and exchangers, and fungal citrate exporters. Curated annotation gives the first three groups substrate-specific descendants: GO:1990961 (xenobiotic detoxification by transmembrane export across the plasma membrane), GO:0010315 (auxin export across the plasma membrane) and GO:0036376 (sodium ion export across plasma membrane). Rules asserting those three terms already cover 7 of the 14 sets (1, 3, 5, 9, 14; 2; 8), which therefore emit nothing here. What the substrate is, is the informative part of an export annotation, and the consequent leaves it out.",
