    "review_summary": "Accuracy: both condition sets were read. Set 1 (IPR003409 (MORN repeat) AND IPR052472 (MORN repeat-containing protein 3) AND PANTHER:PTHR46511:SF1) has no taxon condition; a query on the PANTHER family, an upper bound, returns 1,648 UniProtKB entries, of which 874 are vertebrate, 233 arthropod, 75 Viridiplantae and 25 fungal. The FUNCTION comment the rule assigns names p53/TP53, SIRT1 and MDM2. No Viridiplantae or fungal entry in UniProtKB matches the Mdm2/Mdm4 family, IPR016495 (p53 negative regulator Mdm2/Mdm4), so in those lineages the text describes partners that are not there. The mechanism was shown for mammalian MORN3 (PMID:29681526) and the spermatogenesis role in mouse (PMID:25248657). Meaning and parsimony: the two sets select one unit, the MORN3 family, so the rule is coherent about which proteins it means; the defect is that it attaches a lineage-specific mechanism to the whole family. The construction is also heavier than it needs to be. IPR052472 and PANTHER:PTHR46511 match exactly the same 1,747 entries, so two of the three signatures of set 1 restate each other, and 183 of the 185 eukaryotic entries with the FunFam of set 2 already carry IPR052472. This is a FUNCTION-comment rule, so projects/ARBA_REVIEW/rule_redundancy.tsv has no row for it.",
