    "description": "Assigns GO:0052629 phosphatidylinositol-3,5-bisphosphate 3-phosphatase activity to primate and eukaryotic myotubularin-family proteins through four alternative condition sets: the myotubularin-like phosphatase domain together with the protein-tyrosine phosphatase active site (Primates), and three myotubularin FunFams (Primates, Haplorrhini, Eukaryota).",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all four live condition sets were examined. Every Swiss-Prot entry matching any set carries GO:0052629 (phosphatidylinositol-3,5-bisphosphate 3-phosphatase activity), and each set contains members annotated from experiments (MTMR2, MTMR3, MTMR4, MTMR6, MTMR8, MTM1, MTMR1). In set 1 the active-site condition IPR016130 (Protein-tyrosine phosphatase, active site) is what separates the active myotubularins from the catalytically inactive family members. Meaning and parsimony: the four sets select one biological unit, the catalytically active myotubularins, and the consequent is a leaf term (no descendants) that experiments place on the members themselves, so the rule says the most informative thing that is true of what it selects. Sets 2 and 3 mostly repeat set 1 (239 of 284 and 149 of 157 of their UniProtKB matches also match set 1), which is some redundancy but not sets that do nothing. Three of the four sets are restricted to primates, which follows where the human annotations are and not where the enzyme exists.",
