    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all eight live condition sets were examined. In each set the Swiss-Prot matches carry GO:0032206 (positive regulation of telomere maintenance) or a descendant with experimental evidence: TERF2 (IDA), ATM (IMP), tankyrases (IDA), MAPK1 and MAPK3 (IMP), CCT subunits (IMP), RTEL1 (IMP), mouse RUVBL1 and RUVBL2 (IMP) and SLX4 (IDA). No wrongly annotated protein was found. Meaning and parsimony: the rule is a list of eight unrelated proteins or protein pairs that have each been shown to promote telomere maintenance, by different routes (a shelterin subunit, checkpoint and MAP kinases, a poly-ADP-ribosyltransferase, a chaperonin, helicases, a nuclease scaffold). For four of them (ATM, tankyrase, CCT, RuvB-like helicases) the curated term is a descendant of the consequent, and a separate rule already asserts that descendant with the same signatures, so those four sets emit nothing. For the other four (TERF2, MAPK1/MAPK3, RTEL1, SLX4) the consequent is the curated term itself.",
