    "description": "Assigns 3-oxopropanoate + NADP(+) + CoA = malonyl-CoA + NADPH + H(+) (EC 1.2.1.75) to archaeal proteins matching CATH FunFam 3.40.50.720:FF:000411. The FunFam contains both malonyl-CoA reductases and their aspartate-semialdehyde dehydrogenase paralogs, and the rule has no condition that separates them.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: the rule is right for about half of the proteins it annotates. Of 38 rule-annotated archaeal entries (UniProt, 2026-10-15), 17 match the MCR-type CDD models and are malonyl-CoA reductases, 17 match the archaeal/fungal ASD-type models and are aspartate-semialdehyde dehydrogenases, and 4 match neither. In each genome both paralogs receive the malonyl-CoA reductase reaction. Gene reviews in this repository document both sides: Msed_0709 (the real M. sedula MCR, curated in Swiss-Prot and not rule-annotated) and Msed_1700 (its ASD paralog, misannotated by this rule). Meaning and parsimony: the single condition set selects two enzymes, not one. The FunFam groups the archaeal malonyl-CoA reductases of the 3-hydroxypropionate/4-hydroxybutyrate cycle with the aspartate-semialdehyde dehydrogenases they arose from, and the reaction in the consequent is true of the first unit only. The rule is minimal, one signature plus Archaea, so it fails by having too little condition, not too much.",
