    "review_summary": "Accuracy: both live condition sets were examined. Set 1 matches three Swiss-Prot entries, all laminin subunit beta-2 (human P55268, rat P15800, mouse Q61292); human and mouse LAMB2 are experimentally annotated to GO:0005608 (laminin-121 trimer). Set 2 matches laminin subunit gamma-1 of human (P11047) and mouse (P02468), both annotated to the term by TAS. For these reviewed vertebrate chains the annotation is true. Meaning and parsimony: the sets select two chains of one complex, so the rule is a coherent statement, with two limits. The term names one trimer among many that each chain builds: curated annotation puts human gamma-1 in eleven laminin trimers and beta-2 in nine, and no set selects alpha-1, the chain that distinguishes laminin-121. And the only taxon condition, NOT Fungi, does no work for a metazoan protein family and lets set 1 reach 26 non-vertebrate entries, 21 of them nematode laminin beta chains that QuickGO shows annotated to laminin-121 by this rule. The alpha1, beta2, gamma1 chain nomenclature is defined for vertebrate laminins.",
