    "review_summary": "Accuracy: all five live condition sets were examined. Every Swiss-Prot entry that matches a full conjunction is curated to GO:0051010 (microtubule plus-end binding) itself, and each set has at least one match with experimental evidence: CLIP1 and CLIP2 of mouse and rat (set 1), MAPRE1 of human, mouse and rat (set 2), human CLASP1 and CLASP2 (set 3), S. cerevisiae BIM1 and S. pombe mal3 (set 4), and S. pombe dis1 (set 5; alp14 by TAS). Meaning and parsimony: the five sets resolve into four closely related units, the classic plus-end tracking protein families (CLIP-170, EB, CLASP, XMAP215/Dis1), and the consequent is the most informative function term curators put on all of them; it has no descendants and no set is covered by another rule. Each set does its own work. The one weakness is taxon scope: CLIP is limited to Glires and CLASP to Primates, which reflects where the training annotations are, not where the families exist. That is narrow coverage, not wrong annotation.",
