    "review_summary": "Accuracy: the live rule has one condition set, CATH FunFam 1.20.1730.10:FF:000006 (Urea active transporter) in Fungi. Its Swiss-Prot matches are S. cerevisiae DUR3 (P33413), C. albicans DUR3 (A0A1D8PDB5) and S. pombe dur3-1 (O94469). P33413 has GO:0015606 (spermidine transmembrane transporter activity) by IDA and IMP and A0A1D8PDB5 by IMP; GO:0015606 is part_of GO:1903711 (spermidine transmembrane transport), so the annotation is true of the characterised members. Meaning and parsimony: the set selects one unit, the fungal DUR3 urea and polyamine transporters, and the consequent is an informative statement about it. But the same set is covered by ARBA00089374, which asserts GO:0015606, the molecular function that implies this process by part_of. UniProt keeps the more specific ARBA term, and QuickGO holds no annotation with ARBA:ARBA00089391 as its source (2026-11-12), so the rule does no work.",
    "action": "DEPRECATE",
    "status": "COMPLETE",
