    "description": "Assigns GO:0000055 (ribosomal large subunit export from nucleus) to two groups of budding-yeast ribosomal proteins: ubiquitin-ribosomal protein eL40 fusions in Saccharomycotina, and ribosomal protein uL1 (L10a) in Saccharomycetes. Each condition set requires two CATH FunFams and a taxon.",
    "review_summary": "Accuracy: both live condition sets were examined. Set 2 (ribosomal protein uL1 in Saccharomycetes) is supported: Saccharomyces cerevisiae RPL1A and RPL1B carry GO:0000055 (ribosomal large subunit export from nucleus) with IMP evidence from SGD. Set 1 (ubiquitin-eL40 fusion proteins in Saccharomycotina) has no manual support: RPL40A and RPL40B carry the term only through this rule. Meaning and parsimony: the two sets select two unrelated ribosomal proteins, and the consequent fits only one of them. SGD curates eL40 from the paper that studied its role in 60S biogenesis to GO:0000027 (ribosomal large subunit assembly), which is not under the consequent, and did not annotate export. The rule is small and has no redundant set, but set 1 asserts a process that the curators who read the eL40 literature chose not to assert.",
